---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
---
<InfoPageLayout
  eyebrow="Commercial transparency"
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How HydroRigor will disclose and qualify compensated links if affiliate relationships are introduced later."
  pathname="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' },
    { label: 'Testing Methodology', href: '/testing-methodology/' },
    { label: 'Buyer Guides', href: '/best/' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Current status</h2>
  <p>HydroRigor does not currently publish affiliate links or claim active affiliate relationships. The M03 site contains no affiliate destinations, paid links, live prices, or product feeds.</p>

  <h2>Future disclosure standard</h2>
  <p>If compensated links are introduced in a later authorized milestone, a clear disclosure will appear before or near relevant commercial content. Qualifying purchases may generate compensation without changing the price paid by the reader, but that language will be used only when it accurately reflects an active program's terms.</p>

  <h2>Link qualification</h2>
  <p>Future compensated links must use appropriate relationship attributes and pass through the approved affiliate-link abstraction. HydroRigor will not hide a material connection behind an ordinary editorial link.</p>

  <h2>Editorial separation</h2>
  <p>Compensation must not determine which product is selected, how evidence is described, or what conclusion is reached. Supplied, loaned, or discounted products must be disclosed separately from affiliate compensation.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
